Write a program that will read the amount of money that will be withdrawn from an ATM (e.g. P500 or P1200)
then compute and output the least number of peso bills (P100 peso bills, P500 peso bills, P1000 peso bills) that
will be dispensed by the machine for the requested amount.

Determine also the amount of money corresponding
to each peso bill dispensed, the sum total of number of bills dispensed, and sum total of amounts per
denomination as shown below.

Assume that enough bills are always available from the machine. Assume
further that the machine can only dispense P100 peso bills, P500 peso bills, and P1000 peso bills.
---------------------------------------------------------
Input: Withdraw amount
Processes:  Compute the least number of peso bills to be dispensed in P100, P500 and P1000 bills.
            Compute the amount of money to each peso bill to be dispensed.
            Compute the sum total number of bills dispensed
            Compute the sum total of amounts per denomination
Output:  Bills (P100, P500 and P1000)
        Amount of money dispensed for each peso bill
        Total number of bills dispensed
        Total Amount dispensed per denomination
---------------------------------------------------------
Algorithm:
1. Read the input amount to be withdrawn
2. Compute the least number the machine will withdraw for each peso bill
3. Compute the amount for each peso bill will be dispensed
4. Compute the total number of bills to be dispensed
5. Display results
*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Dispenser{
    public static void main (String[] args){

        //scanner declaration
        Scanner input = new Scanner (System.in);

        //declaration of values
        int withdrawAmount;
        int oneThousands;
        int fiveHundreds;
        int oneHundreds;
        int total1000s;
        int total500s;
        int total100s;
        int totallBills;
        int totalAmounWithdrawn;

        //withdrawAmount input
        System.out.print("Please enter amount to withdraw: ");
        withdrawAmount = input.nextInt();

        //Computing for the number of 1000 bills
        oneThousands = withdrawAmount/1000;
        withdrawAmount %= 1000;

        //compute for the number of 500 bills
        fiveHundreds = withdrawAmount/500;
        withdrawAmount %= 500;

        //compute for the number of 100 bills
        oneHundreds = withdrawAmount/100;

        //compute the amount dispensed for each denomination
        total100s = 100*oneHundreds;
        total500s = 500*fiveHundreds;
        total1000s = 1000*oneThousands;

        //Compute the Total number of bills and total Amount
        totallBills = oneHundreds+fiveHundreds+oneThousands;
        totalAmounWithdrawn = total100s+total500s+total1000s;
        //Display results
        System.out.println("PESO BILLS          QUANTITY     AMOUNT");
        System.out.println("==================================");
        System.out.println("P1000                    " + oneThousands + "             " + total1000s);
        System.out.println("P500                     " + fiveHundreds + "             " + total500s);
        System.out.println("P100                     " + oneHundreds + "             " + total100s);
        System.out.println("----------------------------------");
        System.out.println("Total number of bills    " + totallBills + "             " + totalAmounWithdrawn);
    }
}
